{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones","id":1358170,"title":"Touchstones?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-01T03:44:20-08:00","id":1358170,"title":"Touchstones?","content":"I know mages are human and Touchstones are supposed to be the things that keep inhuman supernaturals grounded. But then look at how werewolves have a Touchstone for both their flesh and spirit sides, granting their Touchstones a different context to how vampires use them. I think mages could use Touchstones in a similar way. Mages may be human, but they experience things most humans don't. Magical awareness tends to isolate them from the common man, especially considering Quiescence. Touchstones could provide an anchor to humanity and aid their Wisdom. Directly causing a Sleeper to experience Quiescence is always an Act of Hubris, but doing it to their Touchstone would provide a powerfully emotional context to their hubris.<br /> <br /> Just an idea at this point, I don't have any hard mechanics on it or even specific examples. I just thought of throwing it out there to see what others think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T04:24:15-08:00","id":1358178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones#post1358170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones could provide an anchor to humanity and aid their Wisdom. Directly causing a Sleeper to experience Quiescence is always an Act of Hubris, but doing it to their Touchstone would provide a powerfully emotional context to their hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I would need a bit more of a sell on this before I'd consider this sort of house rule for myself.<br /> <br /> How does having an anchor to humanity aid your Wisdom? Humanity isn't inherently Wise. A college buddy that made it rich in the stock market before blowing it all on living big, that's rebuilding as a more modest person is, sure a reminder of the dangers of power, and the ability to do better... but the temptations of material wealth pale in comparison to the power magic holds for mages to pridefully grasp.<br /> <br /> There's already plenty of Merits for having significant mortals in your life that don't have to directly hook into Wisdom and get any specific narrative moments with.<br /> <br /> It also seems very hard for a Mage Touchstone to serve it's purpose without losing a lot of the dramatic tension in other games. A vampire's Touchstones generally don't agree to being one, or even know. What the vampire sees in them that helps the vampire connect to Humanity might be a complete fabrication in the vampire's mind that their Touchstone would soundly reject if confronted with it. I don't see how a mage's Touchstone wouldn't have to be much more aware of their role as someone the mage wants in their life to help sort through stuff (even if the Touchstone never finds out what exactly).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T10:49:07-08:00","id":1358222,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to agree with Heavy Arms. A Mage isolating himself from humanity has very little to do with Wisdom. That's more a product of their Obsessions. Like, Harry Dresden is a low-Wisdom Mage, but when he's not on his bullshit he remembers and interacts with regular folks pretty easily. His circle of regular folks is pretty small, and they tend to get slowly drawn into his bullshit if he gets too close to them. A high Wisdom Mage on the other end might be isolated from humanity by virtue of trying to remain in their ivory tower to maintain their control over their magic by not getting into messy situations or needlessly smearing their Nimbus on things. They could choose not to be isolated too though, carefully constructing cults made of soccer moms or something that work to their purposes.<br /> <br /> So isolation is...something else apart from Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Let's look at it another way, even a Mage who maintains high Wisdom is going to become less &quot;human&quot; over the course of their career as their Gnosis increases, they gain legacy attainments, and run the chance, ultimately, of Ascending. Does that prevent them from interacting or being close with people? Only to the extent that they let it. Though yeah, Ascension is kind of a cutoff point that makes it way more difficult to be a regular Joe. Even then they could create Ochemata or something if getting a brew with the boys was that important to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T11:29:46-08:00","id":1358226,"title":"","content":"Look at how the gamelines with Touchstones operate in terms of Integrity-equivalent:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Vampires and changelings literally risk Humanity loss or Clarity damage just from spending too much time without human interaction, period, and their Touchstones in particular keep them from edging closer to frenzy or getting attrition'd into a coma. They're built to be social creatures that interact with humanity on a semiregular basis, or at least have developed odd periodic workarounds to the fact that isolation starts to tilt them a little bit sideways.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Deviants incur Instability over time if they aren't actively pursuing the relationships their Touchstones currently represent, and the only other means they have of restoring their Stability besides aiming down those sights is to roll well with their volatile superpowers, a state that they mostly need to be stable in the first place to cultivate. They start with nearly as many Touchstones as a vampire or changeling can mechanically have and maintaining them is the core focus of the game's default arc to such a degree that &quot;how many Touchstones you still have&quot; is a secondary Integrity analog.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Werewolves start with two Touchstones, can't get more than that, can shift the benefits of one over the other, mostly use them to slow their jump up or down the Harmony scale or quickly correct a shift in the wrong direction, and have a slightly stronger rationale than usual for having their Touchstones be things that aren't creatures. They detach their Touchstones at points near the ends of the scale they're ideally trying to keep to the middle of, which makes it easier for them to get stuck at the ends and effectively trapped in one of the two worlds they inhabit while more susceptible to Death Rage.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Sin-Eaters start with one Touchstone, get another one and then another one as their Synergy rises (which they lose access to if their Synergy falls), naturally raise their Synergy by resolving the issues at the heart of their Touchstones, temporarily raise their Synergy in the pursuit of those issues, and run into trouble when two or more of their Touchstones come into conflict with each other. It's entirely possible for them to deal with their Burden and Remembrance in order and wind up with only one Touchstone left to worry about \u2014 the one that represents their vision for the Underworld \u2014 and in fact this is encouraged by the fact that the only benefit to having multiple Touchstones is being able to pursue both at once for a larger temporary Synergy boost.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Mummies pick up Touchstones electively as a source of Reminisce Beats, and notably they're the only such source that is both inexhaustible and not tied to destroying relics. They are valuable for their impact on the ability to cultivate Memory rather than their utility in staving off its loss, and much of their other benefits are inherited from the other social connections they have to the mummy, like holding their Pillars or being their Sadikh.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hunters (assuming the 2017 preview rules still hold more or less true) have Touchstones in the same model as vampires and changelings do (start with one, pick up more as a Merit, having multiple attached gives you an extra die on breaking point rolls), have converted their Integrity to a Wisdom-esque loosely-tiered set of breaking points that you can be hardened to, need to have a heart-to-heart with their Touchstones to buy back Integrity, roll Resolve + Composure for breaking points with a penalty from the breaking point and bonus from their Touchstone(s) alongside other modifiers, and get a little weird on exceptional successes to keep their Integrity. They're very likely to be under a Persistent Condition that makes them Spooked fairly frequently, and the key concept surrounding their Integrity as a social widget is more or less &quot;trust.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mages already track things and people that are important to them through sympathy, can't meaningfully tell most people about the things they see for reasons that have nothing to do with how important that person is to them, and are host to a power that not only doesn't get worse with isolation but passively steers complications towards their sympathetic connections in a way that is only partially managed by maintaining a separate magical identity to ground those complications towards. In other words, they don't have Touchstones for similar reasons that the Begotten, the Unchained, and the Created don't have Touchstones.<br /> <br /> You'd need to determine what Awakened Touchstones are actually for, because transplanting the rationale from another gameline outright simply doesn't work and in some cases is directly antithetical to how some existing fact of Awakened existence already works \u2014 for example, your first Touchstone in Geist is built around an Aspiration, but Touchstones don't help you maintain Synergy in Geist and Mage's equivalent (Obsessions) is actively detrimental to your Wisdom even as it's necessary for you to buy Wisdom back up. There's more to Touchstones than &quot;thing that keeps your Integrity stat from falling.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T21:28:11-08:00","id":1358348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358178#post1358178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I would need a bit more of a sell on this before I'd consider this sort of house rule for myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I ain't getting into rules at this point. I'm just talking about the validity of the idea. We can go over mechanics afterwards, or not at all depending on the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358178#post1358178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does having an anchor to humanity aid your Wisdom? Humanity isn't inherently Wise. A college buddy that made it rich in the stock market before blowing it all on living big, that's rebuilding as a more modest person is, sure a reminder of the dangers of power, and the ability to do better... but the temptations of material wealth pale in comparison to the power magic holds for mages to pridefully grasp.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much humanity itself is wise that would make the Touchstone aid Wisdom, but rather grounding yourself to the Fallen keeps you from completely descending down the rabbit hole of the Supernal and becoming Enraptured. Besides, the only real difference between the power of money and the power of magic is a matter of degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358178#post1358178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also seems very hard for a Mage Touchstone to serve it's purpose without losing a lot of the dramatic tension in other games. A vampire's Touchstones generally don't agree to being one, or even know. What the vampire sees in them that helps the vampire connect to Humanity might be a complete fabrication in the vampire's mind that their Touchstone would soundly reject if confronted with it. I don't see how a mage's Touchstone wouldn't have to be much more aware of their role as someone the mage wants in their life to help sort through stuff (even if the Touchstone never finds out what exactly).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand what you getting at here exactly. Are you saying that a mage's Touchstones can't function the same way a vampire's Touchstone would? If so, then I'd completely agree. Mages are human, vampires aren't. Therefore, a mage's Touchstone isn't about how a mage connects to their humanity. Instead, their Touchstone keeps them connected to the Fallen World as a whole. Oh sure, the Fallen World is an illusion (at least, from the mage's perspective), but they still live in said illusion and have to interact with it to maintain a healthy degree of sanity. Shutting yourself from that world to your Obsessions puts you on the fast track to being Enraptured.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358222#post1358222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to agree with Heavy Arms. A Mage isolating himself from humanity has very little to do with Wisdom. That's more a product of their Obsessions. Like, Harry Dresden is a low-Wisdom Mage, but when he's not on his bullshit he remembers and interacts with regular folks pretty easily. His circle of regular folks is pretty small, and they tend to get slowly drawn into his bullshit if he gets too close to them. A high Wisdom Mage on the other end might be isolated from humanity by virtue of trying to remain in their ivory tower to maintain their control over their magic by not getting into messy situations or needlessly smearing their Nimbus on things. They could choose not to be isolated too though, carefully constructing cults made of soccer moms or something that work to their purposes.<br /> <br /> So isolation is...something else apart from Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see where you're coming from, but I disagree.<br /> <br /> In the case of Harry Dresden, isolation from ordinary folks isn't the only form of hubris. It's not like I'm arguing about penalizing a low-Wisdom mage's Social rolls or anything. I'm just saying it's a lot easier for your Wisdom to slip when you're not engaging in a social life. Humans are a social species after all. Our mental health relies on a hearty amount of social interaction.<br /> <br /> For the high Wisdom mage in their ivory tower, I'd say living in an ivory tower is a big red flag for their Wisdom. If you sit on a mountain top looking down on a city, it's very easy to lose sight of the city-folks' concerns and well-being. When you're spending all your time on pursuing your Obsessions, it's a lot easier to lose sight of anything outside of them. Sure, the wizard becoming a hermit to attain spiritual enlightenment is a major trope Awakening evokes. However, the hermit pays a price for their isolation. There's a difference between Gnosis and Wisdom. Seeing the big picture has its pros <i>and</i> cons; just like seeing the small picture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358222#post1358222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's look at it another way, even a Mage who maintains high Wisdom is going to become less &quot;human&quot; over the course of their career as their Gnosis increases, they gain legacy attainments, and run the chance, ultimately, of Ascending. Does that prevent them from interacting or being close with people? Only to the extent that they let it. Though yeah, Ascension is kind of a cutoff point that makes it way more difficult to be a regular Joe. Even then they could create Ochemata or something if getting a brew with the boys was that important to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I wasn't too clear in my OP, and that's my bad. I posted it late at night, so I probably miscommunicated a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358226#post1358226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd need to determine what Awakened Touchstones are actually for, because transplanting the rationale from another gameline outright simply doesn't work and in some cases is directly antithetical to how some existing fact of Awakened existence already works \u2014 for example, your first Touchstone in Geist is built around an Aspiration, but Touchstones don't help you maintain Synergy in Geist and Mage's equivalent (Obsessions) is actively detrimental to your Wisdom even as it's necessary for you to buy Wisdom back up. There's more to Touchstones than &quot;thing that keeps your Integrity stat from falling.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point. So here's what Awakened Touchstones represent: it's a connection to a mage's Fallen existence. Mages may have incredible magical insight, but they're still human. Meaning they're social creatures and have to maintain social relationships to stay mentally healthy. A mage who loses sight of this necessity to completely pursue their Obsessions becomes highly vulnerable to being Enraptured by the Mysteries. They do <i>not</i> represent an Awakened's personal humanity, but rather their connection to the rest of humanity. It's a mage's spouse and kids back home, their day job with their fellow employees, or their weekly night out with the buds. They don\u2019t remind the mage of their humanity (merely stubbing their toe could do that); they remind the mage that they live in the Fallen World. That there\u2019s more to life than magic and the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> In the context of storytelling, a mage\u2019s Touchstones serve as an opposite tug to their Obsessions. It presents players with a choice: pursue your Sleeper life or your Awakened life. It encourages the ST to break up the narrative into Awakened and Sleeper contexts. Besides changing things up, it also gives players a sense that their characters are part of a secret world since they\u2019re encouraged to contrast it against their Fallen relations. Hogwarts feels a lot more magical when you have to regularly interact with the muggle world. Touchstones in character creation gets players to think about their character\u2019s mundane life and the Sleepers important to them, which always creates a great asset for the ST (\u201cThe Seers abducted your kids\u201d as an example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 01-02-2020, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T23:27:51-08:00","id":1358359,"title":"","content":"1) The very fact that you're saying they're meant to oppose Obsessions rather than aid Wisdom is a core reason to question why they're Touchstones. Touchstones are a name for something that help your manage your Integrity equivalent, not a generic term for any non-supernatural your character has an important bond with. A mage can have a True Friend without Touchstones being involved.<br /> <br /> 2) The idea that a mage's mental health means socialization isn't bad, but there's no clear reason presented on why it has to be Sleepers. If anything constantly interacting with Sleepers just reinforces how alienated a mage is from most people. They'll never understand what a mage does. Social interaction for mental health requires <b>peers</b>. To that end, a mage's cabal, Order, and Consilium all provide plenty of people to interact with that will actually fulfill their need mental health needs.<br /> <br /> 3) The juxtaposition between Sleeper and Supernal has value, but making it hinge on Touchstones makes it an inherent part of the game, not just a way to tell a different Mage story. Esp. with considerations like sympathetic connections, it has a strong possibility of making Touchstones more millstones around character's necks than empowering the Sleeper lives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T00:16:07-08:00","id":1358366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358359#post1358359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) The very fact that you're saying they're meant to oppose Obsessions rather than aid Wisdom is a core reason to question why they're Touchstones. Touchstones are a name for something that help your manage your Integrity equivalent, not a generic term for any non-supernatural your character has an important bond with. A mage can have a True Friend without Touchstones being involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why can't a Touchstone do both? Besides, I had already established that Touchstones were meant to aid Wisdom. I just didn't wanna repeat myself is all. Besides, Obsessions negatively impact Wisdom. So Touchstones contrasting Obsessions makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358359#post1358359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The idea that a mage's mental health means socialization isn't bad, but there's no clear reason presented on why it has to be Sleepers. If anything constantly interacting with Sleepers just reinforces how alienated a mage is from most people. They'll never understand what a mage does. Social interaction for mental health requires <b>peers</b>. To that end, a mage's cabal, Order, and Consilium all provide plenty of people to interact with that will actually fulfill their need mental health needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The term peer is relative. Just because you've joined a particular group no one else can understand doesn't mean you just stop interacting with those outside the group. People who do are often part of cults. Whether they like it or not, mages are intrinsically connected to the Fallen World. Denying and/or ignoring that connection is gonna lead to problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358359#post1358359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) The juxtaposition between Sleeper and Supernal has value, but making it hinge on Touchstones makes it an inherent part of the game, not just a way to tell a different Mage story.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with making the juxtaposition an inherent part of the game? Mages <i>are</i> that juxtaposition incarnate. So it stands to reason that it should be inherent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358359#post1358359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Esp. with considerations like sympathetic connections, it has a strong possibility of making Touchstones more millstones around character's necks than empowering the Sleeper lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could say the same for a vampire's Touchstones (or any other supernatural's Touchstones, for that matter), and I don't see it as a bad thing. It establishes a character's weak spots, and the ST can challenge a player by exploiting that weakness. That, and Touchstones aren't really changing things up from a setting perspective because an Awakened would already have Sleeper relations anyway. All it really does is give mechanical incentive to focus on the key relations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T00:55:48-08:00","id":1358371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358366#post1358366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why can't a Touchstone do both?</div> </div> </div> </div>A character can serve multiple purposes (which is why you can stack Merits on one NPC, such as a Touchstone Retainer True Friend). A Touchstone is something with a mechanical concept in the CofD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The term peer is relative. </div> </div> </div>But still important to the psychological needs of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because you've joined a particular group no one else can understand doesn't mean you just stop interacting with those outside the group. </div> </div> </div>Well, for mages it tends to on some level, because disconnecting themselves from their past is seen as an important measure for the safety of everyone involved.<br /> <br /> And, of course, most of the Orders actively encourage participation in Sleeper society, just on their terms instead of the characters' old terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Denying and/or ignoring that connection is gonna lead to problems. </div> </div> </div>Nobody is saying otherwise. But not having a Touchstone system doesn't mean these issues are being denied or ignored. You're creating a false dichotomy where somehow we need Touchstones for this even if they're not serving the distinct purposes present in other games. Mages have lots of existing reasons to engage with Sleeper society without Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's wrong with making the juxtaposition an inherent part of the game? </div> </div> </div>The method you're proposing is a very specific mode of play that narrows what Mage is without any real benefit I can see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could say the same for a vampire's Touchstones (or any other supernatural's Touchstones, for that matter), and I don't see it as a bad thing. </div> </div> </div>The other supernaturals that have Touchstones don't have to deal with effects like Nimbus and Sympathy. No matter what your Wisdom, your Nimbus is going to have long-term impacts on anyone you have a Strong connection with; which a Touchstone would likely have to qualify for. That Strong connection also means it's easy to identify such individuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It establishes a character's weak spots, and the ST can challenge a player by exploiting that weakness. </div> </div> </div>Again, we don't need Touchstones just for the ST to come up with ways to mess with the player characters; and really it's not great story fodder because it needs to be done with a light hand as most players don't like having Merits they pay points/XP for to be constantly used against them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T03:13:12-08:00","id":1358386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character can serve multiple purposes (which is why you can stack Merits on one NPC, such as a Touchstone Retainer True Friend). A Touchstone is something with a mechanical concept in the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't see why a Touchstone can't both aid Wisdom and contrast with Obsessions, which can potentially worsen Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still important to the psychological needs of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood me. When I said peer is relative, it's relative to a particular context. As in, a Sleeper can be a peer to an Awakened relative to their humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for mages it tends to on some level, because disconnecting themselves from their past is seen as an important measure for the safety of everyone involved.<br /> <br /> And, of course, most of the Orders actively encourage participation in Sleeper society, just on their terms instead of the characters' old terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt any rational Awakened is gonna completely abandon the Sleepers close to them just to keep them safe, let alone encourage other Awakened to do so. A much more measured response would be to keep them away from their magical double life, instead. It's one of the reasons they use Shadow Names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is saying otherwise. But not having a Touchstone system doesn't mean these issues are being denied or ignored. You're creating a false dichotomy where somehow we need Touchstones for this even if they're not serving the distinct purposes present in other games. Mages have lots of existing reasons to engage with Sleeper society without Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I don't think Touchstones have to be a one-size-fits-all mechanic. I mean, vampire Touchstones work vastly differently to werewolf Touchstones. So why do mage Touchstones have to mimic some other supernatural's Touchstones? Second, game mechanics are all about encouraging specific behaviors from players or presenting them with some kinda choice to decide on. Touchstones would encourage players to pay attention to the Sleeper side of their characters' lives, or force them to prioritize said side or their Obsessions. By presenting gameplay consequences to both choices, players are faced with an interesting dilemma to solve.<br /> <br /> Sure, you don't strictly <i>need</i> Touchstones to do that, but they're certainly useful for creating those situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The method you're proposing is a very specific mode of play that narrows what Mage is without any real benefit I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't make sense. Like I said, mages are part of the Fallen World and have to interact with it on a regular basis whether they like it or not. Giving a player mechanical incentive to do so doesn't narrow what Mage is in the slightest. If anything, it enhances the secret world aspect of Mage by giving players a regular dose of contrast between the Sleeper world and the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other supernaturals that have Touchstones don't have to deal with effects like Nimbus and Sympathy. No matter what your Wisdom, your Nimbus is going to have long-term impacts on anyone you have a Strong connection with; which a Touchstone would likely have to qualify for. That Strong connection also means it's easy to identify such individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be the case even without the Touchstone mechanic. Even if an Awakened's family isn't a Touchstone, it would still be a Strong connection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358371#post1358371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, we don't need Touchstones just for the ST to come up with ways to mess with the player characters; and really it's not great story fodder because it needs to be done with a light hand as most players don't like having Merits they pay points/XP for to be constantly used against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones would be an additional tool in the toolkit, though. Also, I never suggested for constant exploitation, just occasional exploitation. It makes for great drama, but if used too much it starts to grate.<br /> <br /> So if you don't have any objections that differ from what you've already posted, I'm not gonna respond to them anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 01-02-2020, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T04:37:20-08:00","id":1358395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358386#post1358386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see why a Touchstone can't both aid Wisdom and contrast with Obsessions, which can potentially worsen Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't if they hypothetically can or can't, but the practical limits of what can be accomplished.<br /> <br /> Like, I get it that it sucks that you were probably hoping for a more positive response from people and you're not getting that. But you wanted to see what people think, and we're telling you what we think.<br /> <br /> At a certain point it's on you to accept that the elevator pitch isn't landing with anyone responding. Either you can work on actually coming up with a better pitch instead of getting defensive, or move on with whatever lessons you take from all this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you misunderstood me. When I said peer is relative, it's relative to a particular context. As in, a Sleeper can be a peer to an Awakened relative to their humanity. </div> </div> </div>And... what does being peers in humanity matter to the context? A Touchstone is to oppose Obsessions and aid Wisdom, things Sleepers don't have context to really understand or inform on. You've never established how having bonds with Sleepers actually helps, or why they help specifically would come from Sleepers (for the talk of Touchstones not all working the same way, if anything it makes the most sense for Mage Touchstones to come from beings with connects to the Supernal like Spirit Touchstones connect to the Hisil for werewolves).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt any rational Awakened is gonna completely abandon the Sleepers close to them just to keep them safe, let alone encourage other Awakened to do so. A much more measured response would be to keep them away from their magical double life, instead. It's one of the reasons they use Shadow Names. </div> </div> </div>I never said &quot;completely abandon.&quot; But mages clearly move away from their pre-Awakened life a lot. Also?<br /> <br /> &quot;A Shadow Name serves two functions. First, it helps conceal<br /> the mage\u2019s sympathetic name from enemy mages who might<br /> use that knowledge to cast spells on her sympathetically <span style=\"color:#004E6D\">(see p.<br /> 172). </span>More importantly, though, it prevents the mage\u2019s Nimbus<br /> from affecting those who only know her by her Sleeping identity.<br /> So long as the mage practices magic within her Shadow Name,<br /> only those things close to her as a mage (her cabal, sanctum,<br /> apprentices, Dedicated tools, etc.) are affected by her Nimbus.<br /> <br /> A Shadow Name\u2019s protection works best, however, if a mage<br /> avoids using magic in the presence of the loved ones of his Sleeper life. If he allows too much of a connection to form between<br /> his Shadow Name and his un-Awakened family and friends,<br /> they may yet fall under the influence of his magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the book and all. Considering the risks of failing to walk the line here, mages are going to default to erring on the side of detachment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, vampire Touchstones work vastly differently to werewolf Touchstones. </div> </div> </div>They both provide a dice bonus to resisting changes to their respecting Integrity equivalent, and a way to regain Willpower by spending time with your Touchstone(s).<br /> <br /> The rest of the major differences are because Humanity and Harmony are so different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why do mage Touchstones have to mimic some other supernatural's Touchstones? </div> </div> </div>As far as mimicry goes, they'd end up looking most like Humanity Touchstones because Humanity and Wisdom are the two closest ones.<br /> <br /> And if you actually have ideas about how to do them differently, lets hear them. The burden of proof is on you in this situation to show what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Touchstones would encourage players to pay attention to the Sleeper side of their characters' lives, or force them to prioritize said side or their Obsessions. By presenting gameplay consequences to both choices, players are faced with an interesting dilemma to solve. </div> </div> </div>Except mages <b>already live double lives</b> (if not more). There's nothing to encourage. All of this is already in the game as much as possible without getting punitive. This feels like you're doing an air-breathing mermaid problem, where you're introducing a mechanic to solve a problem that didn't need solving because the game already written such that it wasn't a problem until you add this mechanic.<br /> <br /> Frankly, it feels like you want a mechanical cudgel to make players play Mage the way you want to (focusing on balancing double lives) in the face of players that want to play characters dedicated to the Mysteries. It doesn't really sound like you're struggling to have idea of how to bring the conflicts you want to see come up without Touchstones, which means it's safe to infer that you feel the need to force it into the game rather than &quot;encourage&quot; anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't make sense. Like I said, mages are part of the Fallen World and have to interact with it on a regular basis whether they like it or not. Giving a player mechanical incentive to do so doesn't narrow what Mage is in the slightest. </div> </div> </div>In the game as written, my characters can interact with the Fallen World on the terms they pick. They can completely hide their sympathetic name, using alternate IDs and their Shadow Name to keep people away from being connected too strongly to them for their own good, or they can take the risk of maintaining deep bonds to pre-Awakening Sleeper loved ones, or even form ones with post-Awakening Sleepers. There's already drama and conflict built in by Nimbus and Sympathy.<br /> <br /> But making Touchstones, which have to be Sleeper based to contrast with Obsessions means all mages have to operate in the second space or take the penalty for not having Touchstones (which needs to have enough bite to it that people don't just ignore them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if an Awakened's family isn't a Touchstone, it would still be a Strong connection. </div> </div> </div>See above, and why mages distance themselves from their Sleeper families.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if you don't have any objections that differ from what you've already posted, I'm not gonna respond to them anymore. </div> </div> </div>Please, spare the forums this sort of declarative nonsense. I really don't get why people think anything good comes from, &quot;I'm going to stop posting in response to you!&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, you think I wouldn't get the message if you just stopped responding to me that you felt there wasn't more to say? What did you really think this helps with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T10:08:22-08:00","id":1358438,"title":"","content":"Just as a general, cautionary note: don't associate Wisdom with mental health. That's a 1e thing in all the lines that 2e got rid of pretty successfully and we really don't need it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T12:08:06-08:00","id":1358461,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say you can't associate them, because they still are for many splats.<br /> <br /> What 2e has purged from 1e is the idea that losing your Integrity stat's rating causes specific mental illnesses. And that's for the better. Doing things that cause excessive stress, and thus reduce your mental health, frequently also risk your Integrity stat. And that's fine to keep in.<br /> <br /> A mage that allows their Obsessions to dominate their life - which isn't good for their mental health - is going to struggle to maintain their Wisdom. That's already part of the game. As long as it stays firmly as &quot;not taking care of your psychological needs in one area of your life can negatively impact your ability to maintain your psychological needs in others,&quot; it's not running afoul of what 1e did so poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T17:00:56-08:00","id":1358500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358395#post1358395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, I get it that it sucks that you were probably hoping for a more positive response from people and you're not getting that. But you wanted to see what people think, and we're telling you what we think.<br /> <br /> At a certain point it's on you to accept that the elevator pitch isn't landing with anyone responding. Either you can work on actually coming up with a better pitch instead of getting defensive, or move on with whatever lessons you take from all this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's more like just you that's responding negatively here.<br /> <br /> Mrmdubois agreed with you, granted. However, that was in response to my OP, which I already admitted was a late-night post so I wasn't being the most clear. Also, the concept wasn't as refined as it is now. So at this point, his criticism is already answered.<br /> <br /> Satchel provided very valuable information on how Touchstones work for other gamelines and made the point that Awakened Touchstones have to be more than simply something that aids their Integrity analogue. Which, as I pointed out, was a good point and I refined the concept accordingly.<br /> <br /> Errol216 left a cautionary note to not equate Wisdom with mental health, which is a fair point and duly noted.<br /> <br /> You, on the other hand, may have raised some valid criticisms that helped me to refine Awakened Touchstones, but now it seems like you're just raising objections for the sake of it. Especially considering that you're responding to my refutations to said objections by repeating them. I'm not trying to force Touchstones into your game, I'm just exploring the validity of a concept. If you don't like the concept, you're free to not use it.<br /> <br /> Now, if you have something <i>else</i> to say, then let's hear it. If not, then feel free to ignore the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T18:17:42-08:00","id":1358509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358500#post1358500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it's more like just you that's responding negatively here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only is this not true, you have a whole history we can point at to clarify just how much your response here is part of a trend.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:42:39-08:00","id":1358535,"title":"","content":"Arms has brought up the main other thing I'd thought to say, which is that proper maintenance of your Shadow Name is the primary means of doing what you seem to want Touchstones to accomplish \u2014 the thing about Wisdom and the Awakened is that it's there as a measure of how well you're able to moderate yourself away from the extremes of Obsession and how concerned you are for the consequences of being a magical actor.<br /> <br /> In other words, the problem mages face is not the problem monsters with Touchstones face \u2014 they aren't dealing with intrusive thoughts from alien parapsychology or a the significance of things on the borders of a driving purpose or the flailing attempts of a broken soul to find stability, they're humans who've made themselves into conduits for unadulterated god-magic that is dangerous but thrilling to use, which means they're struggling to various degrees with managing an addiction rather than holding themselves together on a day-to-day level.<br /> <br /> A healthy priority for the Awakened is keeping the supernatural as far away from any mundane life they care about and/or cultivating enough discipline that they can let incidental contact with specimens of the occult go instead of diving into scrutiny and experimentation, which if anything suggests the thing you want to do to encourage mundane living is set up something like Hunter's Persistent Conditions with an early-exit clause of &quot;gain a dot of Wisdom.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T08:09:52-08:00","id":1358622,"title":"","content":"I agree with the Shadow Name idea. Mages have nothing fundamentally driving them away from humanity, nor do they posses natures that they need to balance against it.<br /> <br /> Wisdom represents how careful a mage is, how precise their with their spells and mindful of the consequences. Its not related to how nice they are is or even their emotional state. When they don't exert this control regularly, then the small warps in reality they subconsciously generate spread farther.<br /> <br /> So what they can do is separate their mage and mundane personas. Barring emergencies, plus the occasional Knowing or Unveiling spells, they should avoid casting whenever they use their Sympathetic Name. Those that further cultivate this separation gain merits like Shadow Name. But that is entirely up to the mage.<br /> <br /> But that is exactly the challenge, all of those stem from the mage. Wisdom is a personal restraint they enforce by consistently being more precise, optimal, knowing when not to cast or when to back away before going too far chasing an Obsession. Meaningful interaction with a Touchstone cannot teach any of this to a mage. <br /> <br /> Their mundane Touchstones can help ground them in the Fallen world (although not exclusively, the ghost of a departed person they cared about could do so as well), it can help them decompress, foster character growth and this can certainly be a source of normal beats. But its not related to instilling the wish or skillset needed to be Wise, its more likely that there is an Order or Consilia appointed specialist for that (probably a Guardian or Arrow for the Consilia, rarely a Ladder).<br /> <br /> So what you can do is make these meaninful people or objects/memories provide them with a chance to end (or temporarily suppress, in case of the permanent versions) the Rampant or Melalomaniac conditions via significant interaction, stopping the destructive spiral. The Wisdom specialist could let them earn the beats needed to buy back said Wisdom via lessons. That way you could throw a mundane lifeline to allow a hubristic character to find their balance again, which I believe is what you are looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-03-2020, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T09:22:36-08:00","id":1358630,"title":"","content":"The whole mage Wisdom specialist idea could be interesting with including the skills to bond Goetic familiars to mages that are hand picked for their positive influence on Wisdom and to the personality of the mage that needs help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T10:46:31-08:00","id":1358648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358630#post1358630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole mage Wisdom specialist idea could be interesting with including the skills to bond Goetic familiars to mages that are hand picked for their positive influence on Wisdom and to the personality of the mage that needs help.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the type of aid a Clavicularius or a member of the Concord of Serpents would be eager to provide. <br /> <br /> Another option is a Mind 2 spell. Its like a more restrictive version of telekinesis. When it detects the target thinking of doing something that the caster would recognize as an Act of Hubris (restricted by their Wisdom tier), it opens a telepathic conversation between them. With conjunctional Time 3 <br /> it accelerates their speed of thought to carry it out in moments, should they wish it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T11:05:42-08:00","id":1358654,"title":"","content":"A Sleepwalker with the Ritual Martyr Merit is also a way for a Mage to be confronted with their Hubris. Ultimate magic guilt trip mom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T01:49:10-08:00","id":1359668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358535#post1358535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arms has brought up the main other thing I'd thought to say, which is that proper maintenance of your Shadow Name is the primary means of doing what you seem to want Touchstones to accomplish \u2014 the thing about Wisdom and the Awakened is that it's there as a measure of how well you're able to moderate yourself away from the extremes of Obsession and how concerned you are for the consequences of being a magical actor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how maintaining your Shadow Name would do that, though. I mean, I want to use Touchstones as a mechanical incentive for maintaining one's connections to the Sleepers important to them. A good example of a Touchstone would be Nax's husband Sam from Long Distance in Signs of Sorcery. It gives Nax's player an incentive to turn the radio off to spend the night with their character's hubby.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358535#post1358535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, the problem mages face is not the problem monsters with Touchstones face \u2014 they aren't dealing with intrusive thoughts from alien parapsychology or a the significance of things on the borders of a driving purpose or the flailing attempts of a broken soul to find stability, they're humans who've made themselves into conduits for unadulterated god-magic that is dangerous but thrilling to use, which means they're struggling to various degrees with managing an addiction rather than holding themselves together on a day-to-day level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that managing an addiction, especially one that you can't get rid of, requires one to hold themselves together on a day-to-day basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358535#post1358535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A healthy priority for the Awakened is keeping the supernatural as far away from any mundane life they care about and/or cultivating enough discipline that they can let incidental contact with specimens of the occult go instead of diving into scrutiny and experimentation, which if anything suggests the thing you want to do to encourage mundane living is set up something like Hunter's Persistent Conditions with an early-exit clause of &quot;gain a dot of Wisdom.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you mean with that example. That said, getting a Mundane Beat to ignore one of your Obsessions for the sake of spending time with a Touchstone is the reward I was thinking of using. It feels more like a carrot than a stick if the player doesn't lose out on Experience for spending time in the Fallen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358622#post1358622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what they can do is separate their mage and mundane personas. Barring emergencies, plus the occasional Knowing or Unveiling spells, they should avoid casting whenever they use their Sympathetic Name. Those that further cultivate this separation gain merits like Shadow Name. But that is entirely up to the mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the Shadow Name Merit was a means of enhancing one's magical persona so they could use it as a Yantra, not cultivating the separation between their Fallen and Awakened personas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358622#post1358622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is exactly the challenge, all of those stem from the mage. Wisdom is a personal restraint they enforce by consistently being more precise, optimal, knowing when not to cast or when to back away before going too far chasing an Obsession. Meaningful interaction with a Touchstone cannot teach any of this to a mage.<br /> <br /> Their mundane Touchstones can help ground them in the Fallen world (although not exclusively, the ghost of a departed person they cared about could do so as well), it can help them decompress, foster character growth and this can certainly be a source of normal beats. But its not related to instilling the wish or skillset needed to be Wise, its more likely that there is an Order or Consilia appointed specialist for that (probably a Guardian or Arrow for the Consilia, rarely a Ladder).</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not meant to teach Wisdom, that's what the &quot;Become wiser&quot; Obsession is for. A mage who keeps themselves grounded to the Fallen world ensures the grasp of their empathy to Sleepers, thus having an easier time maintaining Wisdom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1358622#post1358622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you can do is make these meaninful people or objects/memories provide them with a chance to end (or temporarily suppress, in case of the permanent versions) the Rampant or Melalomaniac conditions via significant interaction, stopping the destructive spiral. The Wisdom specialist could let them earn the beats needed to buy back said Wisdom via lessons. That way you could throw a mundane lifeline to allow a hubristic character to find their balance again, which I believe is what you are looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm going for. I'm going for a mechanical incentive to keep mage characters coming back to their Fallen lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T02:55:46-08:00","id":1359674,"title":"","content":"Giving Beats for hanging out with your non-plot related friends and family is an incredibly bad design idea.<br /> <br /> Wisdom is the only thing you can't get if you don't have Arcane Beats. You can't get as many Praxis spells, but you can get up to 10 with normal Beats, and Legacy Attainments only need Arcane Beats if you don't have a tutor.<br /> <br /> So you have just incentivized the players to not participate in the plot. They can sit around hanging out with their Touchstones, do a bit of magical practice as a group on the weekends, and farm Beats until they're the masters of the universe in terms of power level.<br /> <br /> This is one of the differences between writing fiction, where a neat little romantic scene can work easily as a break in the action, and an RPG, where you want to keep things moving because that sort of scene eats into time not really playing the game.<br /> <br /> Less hyperbolic, this idea has the inverse effect of the stated desire of having Touchstones contrast Obsessions and help Wisdom. Normal Beats can't help Wisdom. It's one of the key dramatic tensions in Mage. Learning to be Wise means putting your Wisdom on the line. The best way to learn how to act properly to is go out and risk hubris so you can learn it first hand. A mage that spends all their time delving into the magical can generate Arcane Beats and buy Wisdom, even if they risk losing some Wisdom too. A mage that sits around with their normal-Beat-generating-Touchstones can't raise their Wisdom, as they learn nothing about actually balancing their lives.<br /> <br /> Because an important thing? Empathy has nothing to do with Wisdom. A character with very poor empathy for Sleepers (like a lot of the Silver Ladder) can still act Wise, because they are motivated by the abstract consequences of their actions rather than actually caring about the feelings of normal folks that would get hurt along the way.<br /> <br /> As well, Mage has lots of mechanical incentives to keep mages coming back to their Fallen lives. They're just opt in instead of automatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T17:06:05-08:00","id":1359803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359674#post1359674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving Beats for hanging out with your non-plot related friends and family is an incredibly bad design idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you play a game that makes Mage all about the magical side of a mage's life while ignoring the mundane aspects of such a life and the internal tension these can create for the mage. In a game which centers on this aspect of what it is to BE a mage in relation to existence in a Sleeping society, this offers a chance for mages to not feel penalized by a lack of experience gains due to spending time dealing with this aspect of mage life.<br /> <br /> An example: A character in our Dark Eras game is a mage and a princess; she has to deal with the internal tension her role as a mage plays on her royal duties and how it affects her subjects' lives and fortunes. Having advisors in the form of friends and family outside of mage circles helps keep her grounded and remind her of her higher duty, both magically and in mundane life: service to the needs of her people. She gains a Wisdom benefit from maintaining those connections (+1 on degeneration rolls), provided she spends a scene interacting with such advisors during the story. In essence, they help her check herself before she wrecks herself and her nation both. She balances the Arcane Beat loss of time taken with Sleeping counselors when she could be pursuing the Mysteries with a Common Beat gain for engaging in this interaction and maintaining those connections. Wisdom is benefited in the equation without any decrease in the number of times she risks degeneration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359674#post1359674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wisdom is the only thing you can't get if you don't have Arcane Beats. You can't get as many Praxis spells, but you can get up to 10 with normal Beats, and Legacy Attainments only need Arcane Beats if you don't have a tutor.<br /> <br /> So you have just incentivized the players to not participate in the plot. They can sit around hanging out with their Touchstones, do a bit of magical practice as a group on the weekends, and farm Beats until they're the masters of the universe in terms of power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, you haven't; you've given an opportunity for the plot to become more personal to the characters by incorporating those Sleeping world interactions into it. Those interactions can become vectors for the ST to provide Clues at the same time as they offer aid to Wisdom and a chance for Common Beats (which can be scarce in a Mage game that focuses totally on the magical side of a mage's life). All it involves is a slight re-jig to the ST's thinking; and if the ST can't manage that, then I'd have to wonder how good an ST they really are.<br /> <br /> Like all rules, anything can be gamed; but if the ST is letting such a rule be used by players to sit on their magical asses doing nothing of consequence, then the ST is failing to get either the game or this variant rule idea for it. It's not being suggested as a way to turn gaming sessions into Sleeping world love-ins; it's being suggested as a way to incentivize playing a real, three-dimensional character rather than a one-dimensional caricature. Real world people are not just one thing: they have real-world connections and friendships which have real world impacts on their understandings and choices. For a fully realized game experience, I'd say that mage characters should have no less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359674#post1359674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the differences between writing fiction, where a neat little romantic scene can work easily as a break in the action, and an RPG, where you want to keep things moving because that sort of scene eats into time not really playing the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the scene's 'not really playing the game', then that's the ST's fault. After all, it's the ST's job to incorporate the players' characters, backstories and connections into the plot. If you think the player is using their Sleeping connections to avoid mage life, then shake it up by throwing their mage life right in their face in the middle of such an interaction. Drop a supernatural occurrence into the interaction, or a critical clue to a Mystery; or hell, maybe even a full-blown supernatural battle. Moves the plot along nicely, and also gives the situation serious stakes: you could easily end up losing your Touchstone in such a circumstance, and that says goodbye to the benefit on degeneration rolls that they provided. Suddenly, hiding behind the Touchstone to game the system for free Beats doesn't seem such a brilliant idea...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359674#post1359674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less hyperbolic, this idea has the inverse effect of the stated desire of having Touchstones contrast Obsessions and help Wisdom. Normal Beats can't help Wisdom. It's one of the key dramatic tensions in Mage. Learning to be Wise means putting your Wisdom on the line. The best way to learn how to act properly to is go out and risk hubris so you can learn it first hand. A mage that spends all their time delving into the magical can generate Arcane Beats and buy Wisdom, even if they risk losing some Wisdom too. A mage that sits around with their normal-Beat-generating-Touchstones can't raise their Wisdom, as they learn nothing about actually balancing their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the benefit to Wisdom here is not found in the Beats side of things; they're the compensation to incentivize playing out the Sleeping portion of your character's world. The benefit here is found in reduced degeneration risk; the added layer of perspective forces the mage to see the world from more than just a mage's viewpoint, and thus gives them extra checks and balances when they DO risk Hubris. They learn better because they learn from more than just those who think like themselves. Just as in real life: interactions outside of our own little cliques can teach us startlingly new ways to consider moral and ethical conundrums, and stop us from making mistakes that would have been inevitable if we only listened to the advice of our peers. Mages can (and I would say, SHOULD) benefit greatly from going the extra mile to see the world through Sleeping eyes as well as Supernal ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359674#post1359674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because an important thing? Empathy has nothing to do with Wisdom. A character with very poor empathy for Sleepers (like a lot of the Silver Ladder) can still act Wise, because they are motivated by the abstract consequences of their actions rather than actually caring about the feelings of normal folks that would get hurt along the way.<br /> <br /> As well, Mage has lots of mechanical incentives to keep mages coming back to their Fallen lives. They're just opt in instead of automatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a character who doesn't interact with their Sleeping lives is significantly less likely to act Wise, because they don't care about the way an entire portion of the world sees reality and would be affected by their choices. And the person who won't see the world from the other guy's perspective is ALWAYS going to be more vulnerable to Wisdom loss than the person that takes the effort to do so. This variant rule gives a mechanic to such a commitment; the Common Beat benefit doesn't break the game unless the ST is reckless enough to let it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T17:53:57-08:00","id":1359812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359668#post1359668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how maintaining your Shadow Name would do that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>By definition, your Shadow Name only provides its insulation for the mundane side of your life if you keep it separate from the sympathies of magical actors, most controllably yourself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would argue that managing an addiction, especially one that you can't get rid of, requires one to hold themselves together on a day-to-day basis. </div> </div> </div>With the exception of very minor adjustments developed electively through mystical insight, a mage is not walking corpse dependent upon blood for sustenance, a regenerating berserker demigod scion of a bygone era, a scarred survivor of life in a reality-warping playground for the gods, or a half-dead revenant sharing spiritual real-estate with a powerful and driven ghost. Mages are addicted to mystery in the sense that magic feels good to use and experience, not in the sense that they have become constitutionally dependent upon that rush on a basic level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure what you mean with that example. </div> </div> </div>Hunter 2e's 2017 preview for Integrity runs, essentially, &quot;at Integrity 1-6 you have a Persistent Condition that incentivizes you to follow up on signs of supernatural presence or danger and risk Willpower in service of your Vice or Virtue; you get the Spooked Condition the first time in a chapter that you fail a perception or Empathy-based roll, and you get Beats when you alienate normal people and other hunters in the pursuit of your Vigil.&quot; It makes hunters increasingly paranoid and driven to seek out signs of the supernatural as they drop in Integrity unless they spend scenes opening up to people to justify re-reraising the Trait.<br /> <br /> If you want mages spending time away from the Mysteries, a similar cycle of &quot;detox&quot; may be wise to make available. As it stands, the nearest thing to such a cycle is that the two Conditions an Act of Hubris most typically inflicts effectively operate like Vampire's &quot;the frenzy lasts until you risk losing Humanity&quot; dramatic failure results for frenzy \u2014 the consequences of Wisdom loss are harder to shake off if your limits are higher, you avoid circumstances where you're likely to suffer a Paradox, and/or you have people important to you that you might bring harm to, and in the meantime those consequences are twisting your Obsessions around in a way that more powerful characters are better equipped to just let ride.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always thought the Shadow Name Merit was a means of enhancing one's magical persona so they could use it as a Yantra, not cultivating the separation between their Fallen and Awakened personas. </div> </div> </div>The entire benefit of the Merit aside from a Yantra is that your dots in it serve as a minimum sympathetic Withstand for spells targeting you and therefore you're harder to find or affect outside of your Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-08-2020, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-08T23:32:34-08:00","id":1359848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1358170-touchstones?p=1359803#post1359803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only if you play a game that makes Mage all about the magical side of a mage's life while ignoring the mundane aspects of such a life and the internal tension these can create for the mage. In a game which centers on this aspect of what it is to BE a mage in relation to existence in a Sleeping society, this offers a chance for mages to not feel penalized by a lack of experience gains due to spending time dealing with this aspect of mage life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with the mechanical incentives of granting Beats for spending time with your Touchstones would create.<br /> <br /> In my games? ~85% of long term Aspirations have related to the Fallen World and the mages lives therein, and usually it's a 50/50 split between Sleeper society and mage society short term aspirations. I don't even have to pressure for this to be the case.<br /> <br /> But what it means, is what players get their Beats from fulfilling their Aspirations from balancing both sides of their lives, it's been worked into the plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She gains a Wisdom benefit from maintaining those connections (+1 on degeneration rolls), provided she spends a scene interacting with such advisors during the story. </div> </div> </div>This part still doesn't contradict the issues I raised. As well it's already basically how the rules work since you get a +1 to your degeneration rolls made in defense of your Virtue, which it seems your princess is certainly doing in this example. An additional +1 because she spends time with her Sleeper advisors would be a significant bonus and all, but it doesn't actually make sense narratively as to where that bonus comes from; which multiple people have pointed out now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She balances the Arcane Beat loss of time taken with Sleeping counselors when she could be pursuing the Mysteries with a Common Beat gain for engaging in this interaction and maintaining those connections. </div> </div> </div>Again it fails to address the point. Your princess spends her time being a princess and gets extra Beats, instead of actually dealing with Mysteries, which is what the game is about.<br /> <br /> Are all the other mages in her cabal just leaving her behind to go on magical investigations, netting them Arcane and normal Beats for more than the one she gets for sitting around administering her nation? Or are they stuck waiting for her to finish, at which point everyone just goes off and does something that doesn't move the plot forward until they all have time to go be mages again... where they just earned a Beat for not actually doing anything Beat-worthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, you haven't; you've given an opportunity for the plot to become more personal to the characters by incorporating those Sleeping world interactions into it. </div> </div> </div>You get the Beat whether that's the case or not, so this doesn't counter the point either.<br /> <br /> Going back to my own thing above... Aspirations do this, and ensure that they're actively pursued because you can't sit around and get them, you have to go out and complete them. If your players want to focus on Sleeper world stuff, they'll naturally take Aspirations that relate to it. If they don't... that's clearly not the part of the game they're as interested in playing.<br /> <br /> This is what I meant by there being opt-in parts of the game that already do this stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those interactions can become vectors for the ST to provide Clues... </div> </div> </div>So can literally anything the ST wants. There's nothing special here that makes it better for dropping clues towards Mysteries, and actually worse because interacting with clues means popping out magic, which you don't want to do around your Sleeper family/friends/etc. So now the PCs have to jump through some hoops before they can actually get to the clue in question in a meaningful way.<br /> <br /> [quote]All it involves is a slight re-jig to the ST's thinking; and if the ST can't manage that, then I'd have to wonder how good an ST they really are.[/quote<br /> <br /> I'd estimate between x50 to x75 better than you when they're at their worst and you're at your best. I mean, they're clearly not wasting their time bashing you.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, you wanna know why you're insulting them is actually just a bad reflection on you?<br /> <br /> Because what it means is they're off playing the game collaboratively with their players, instead of here making up house rules that seem to be all about, &quot;how to make everyone playing play carapcarp's preferred way.&quot; You seem to think you've got some creative genius in this... but it's just a tool to railroad the game into a specific playstyle. It's not going to give people some epiphany of how to be better STs by encouraging bad habits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like all rules, anything can be gamed; but if the ST is letting such a rule be used by players to sit on their magical asses doing nothing of consequence, then the ST is failing to get either the game or this variant rule idea for it. </div> </div> </div>So... why isn't this true of STs and making sure that the Fallen World and Sleeper society are important parts of the game without needing a mechanical incentive? If STs aren't making those things part of the game in an interesting fashion, how will your house rule help vs. actually working on making it more interesting to play with those parts of the setting?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not being suggested as a way to turn gaming sessions into Sleeping world love-ins; it's being suggested as a way to incentivize playing a real, three-dimensional character rather than a one-dimensional caricature. </div> </div> </div>And the problem is the mechanical incentive is to turn gaming sessions into Sleeping world love-ins, while doing nothing to actually incentivize deeper characters.<br /> <br /> If players aren't making more than 1-D caricatures despite concept, Path, Order, Virtue/Vice, Aspirations, an Obsession, a dedicated Tool, a Shadow Name, and a Nimbus (and that's just the automatic stuff every default starting mage has... they can get more too)... what is adding another element to help add depth to the character really going to do? One more thing isn't going to suddenly open someone's eyes towards making fuller characters (assuming they're not already doing that, since the whole dissing of people you're doing comes off as judgemental BS instead of accurate observations of people playing the game).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a fully realized game experience, I'd say that mage characters should have no less. </div> </div> </div>Mages have more connections by default than core CofD humans do. Do normal mortal folks need more traits to connect them to the world to be full characters? No. Because you're equivocating between &quot;real world&quot; as in how people operate in our world, and &quot;Fallen World vs Mage Society,&quot; while forgetting that most humans get by just fine without a being forced into a double life.<br /> <br /> A person from a rural community that goes to the big city for college/university, and flourishes in academia as they decide to work towards higher degrees and employment in that area, losing touch with all their old friends and barely keeping up with their family because they have a choice now, and instead spend all their time with their new friends and chosen family is not a lesser person because they &quot;forgot where they came from,&quot; or some BS like that. Playing that sort of character doesn't mean you're not playing a 3-D fully realized character. But you're asserting that a mage who does that is inherently not a full character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the scene's 'not really playing the game', then that's the ST's fault. </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, for adopting a house rule that runs contrary to the flow of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you think the player is using their Sleeping connections to avoid mage life, then shake it up by throwing their mage life right in their face in the middle of such an interaction. </div> </div> </div>So, again, why do I need Touchstones if I can just do this but in the reverse of Sleeper stuff intruding on mage time?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suddenly, hiding behind the Touchstone to game the system for free Beats doesn't seem such a brilliant idea </div> </div> </div>Nah, it just comes off as the ST being a dick for giving you a widget to play with, and then punishing you for playing with it instead of the other things in the game.<br /> <br /> Like I said, giving Beats for hanging out with Touchstones is a bad design. I didn't say connecting Beats to Touchstones couldn't work. It just needs to be part of the plot of the game. If you design a rule where the players just using it as written requires the ST to step in and force them to stop with plot-contrivance.. maybe it's just a bad rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the added layer of perspective forces the mage to see the world from more than just a mage's viewpoint, and thus gives them extra checks and balances when they DO risk Hubris. </div> </div> </div>This, still, doesn't make any coherent sense as a concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They learn better because they learn from more than just those who think like themselves. </div> </div> </div>Mages, and all the crazy entities they interact with, are a plethora of perspectives and different ways of thinking that's a galaxy of options compared to a single moon's options of just humans.<br /> <br /> Mages can go out and actually interact with beings that don't just think slightly differently from them, but completely alien to how humans think. That's more perspective broadening by far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages can (and I would say, SHOULD) benefit greatly from going the extra mile to see the world through Sleeping eyes as well as Supernal ones. </div> </div> </div>The problem here is that you seem really dead set on the idea that mages think fundamentally different from normal humans when... they don't.<br /> <br /> You're treating Awakening like having your human eyes ripped out and replaced with mage eyes that are completely different.<br /> <br /> But the game is setup so that Awakening is like having laser eye surgery where your human eyes are adjusted to see a new dimension to the world on top of what they could see before.<br /> <br /> Mages already see the world though Sleeping eyes, because mage eyes are Sleeping eyes plus, not something radically different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But a character who doesn't interact with their Sleeping lives is significantly less likely to act Wise, because they don't care about the way an entire portion of the world sees reality and would be affected by their choices. </div> </div> </div>Wisdom doesn't care. As long as the mage pays attention to the consequences of their actions knowing that responsibly weight those consequences is essential, they don't have to care about how all those people exist and see things. As I said, Wisdom is not empathy based. A mage that doesn't do something out of a deeply held sense of compassion for Sleepers, and a mage that doesn't do something because they intellectually process the dangerous of the consequences are both acting Wisely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the person who won't see the world from the other guy's perspective is ALWAYS going to be more vulnerable to Wisdom loss than the person that takes the effort to do so. </div> </div> </div>Why? The book doesn't define things this way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T10:25:36-08:00","id":1359916,"title":"","content":"Been a minute, just going to chime in with, Wisdom doesn't care about empathy, or require you to consider things from anyone else's perspective. Wisdom is about being in control of yourself and your actions through not engaging in self-deception, and being aware of the consequences of your actions. You can do terrible things that will make all the Sleepers recoil in horror and still be Wise. Interacting with Sleepers, or anyone else for that matter is not a guarantor of maintaining Wisdom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}